{
  "info": {
    "name": "SafeGate",
    "description": "Postman collection for the SafeGate file-scanning API.\n\nSet the `baseUrl` variable (default: http://localhost:8443) and the `apiKey` variable to match your SAFEGATE_API_KEY environment variable.\n\nEndpoints:\n- GET  /health          – public liveness check (no auth required)\n- POST /api/v1/scan     – upload and scan a file\n- OPTIONS /api/v1/scan  – CORS pre-flight\n\nSecurity features tested:\n- Security headers (HSTS, CSP, X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, etc.)\n- X-Request-ID tracing on every response\n- Rate limiting (429 Too Many Requests)\n- CORS with configurable allowed origins\n- API key authentication (X-API-Key or Bearer token)\n\nDistributed features (requires etcd):\n- Scan result caching – identical files return cached results with '(cached)' in the message\n- Distributed rate limiting – shared state across multiple pods",
    "_postman_id": "safegate-collection-v1",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8443",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "apiKey",
      "value": "changeme",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check – 200 OK",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Body has status healthy', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('healthy');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.service).to.eql('safegate');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.time).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Security headers present', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Content-Type-Options')).to.eql('nosniff');",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Frame-Options')).to.eql('DENY');",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Request-ID')).to.be.a('string').with.lengthOf(32);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Health check – 200 without API key (public endpoint)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200 – /health bypasses auth', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Body has status healthy', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('healthy');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
